{"name":"Beru","hex":"#bfe4d4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Beru (atoll)","blocks":[{"text":"Beru is an atoll in the Southern Gilbert Islands in the Pacific Ocean, part of the Republic of Kiribati. Beru was previously known as Eliza, Francis Island, Maria, Peroat, Peru Island or Sunday. It is part of a larger reef with the Nuka Lagoon at its center, and the nearest island is Nikunau. The Tabiang Lagoon is present in the north. Beru is home to 2,051 inhabitants. Due to sea surges, the atoll is experiencing coastal erosion along with damages to seawalls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Beru_Kiribati.jpg/330px-Beru_Kiribati.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beru_(atoll)","wikidata":"Q613386"},{"title":"Beru (company)","blocks":[{"text":"BERU Group is a listed public company since October 1997. The company was founded as a spark plug factory by Julius Behr and Albert Ruprecht in 1912. The company is the leading manufacturer of diesel cold start systems with an estimated worldwide market share of 40 % for glow plugs. In the field of ignition technology for petrol engines, BERU is one of the four major manufacturers in Europe. BERU makes electronics for cars. The company also produces sensor technology and ignition systems for the oil and gas burner industry. Almost all OE-manufacturers of automobiles, commercial vehicles and engines are BERU's customers. The company's headquarters are located in Ludwigsburg, Germany. BERU was acquired by BorgWarner in 2010."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Mid_20th_century_Beru_spark_plug_175_18_U2_Ludwigsburg_Germany.jpg/330px-Mid_20th_century_Beru_spark_plug_175_18_U2_Ludwigsburg_Germany.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beru_(company)","wikidata":"Q893518"},{"title":"Beru (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Beru (transl. Root) is a 2005 Indian Kannada language satirical film directed by P. Sheshadri starring Suchendra Prasad, H. G. Dattatreya, Neethu and M. P. Venkatarao."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Beru_Film_Poster.jpg/330px-Beru_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beru_(film)","wikidata":"Q16247057"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/GilbertIslandsPos.png/500px-GilbertIslandsPos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/GilbertIslandsPos.png/1280px-GilbertIslandsPos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/GilbertIslandsPos.png/500px-GilbertIslandsPos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGilbertIslandsPos.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/P._Sheshadri_receiving_the_National_Film_Award_for_Best_Feature_Film_in_Kannada_for_Beru.jpg/500px-P._Sheshadri_receiving_the_National_Film_Award_for_Best_Feature_Film_in_Kannada_for_Beru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/P._Sheshadri_receiving_the_National_Film_Award_for_Best_Feature_Film_in_Kannada_for_Beru.jpg/1280px-P._Sheshadri_receiving_the_National_Film_Award_for_Best_Feature_Film_in_Kannada_for_Beru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/P._Sheshadri_receiving_the_National_Film_Award_for_Best_Feature_Film_in_Kannada_for_Beru.jpg/500px-P._Sheshadri_receiving_the_National_Film_Award_for_Best_Feature_Film_in_Kann